The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (rm != ARM_R0)
    emit(ARM_MOV_R(ARM_R0, rm), ctx);
if (rn != ARM_R1)
    emit(ARM_MOV_R(ARM_R1, rn), ctx);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because when `emit_udiv()` is called with `rn` set to `ARM_R0` (r_scratch) and `rm` is loaded into `ARM_R0` first, it results in both the dividend and divisor being the same (both referencing `ARM_R0`). This leads to incorrect behavior during division operations.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (rn != ARM_R1)
    emit(ARM_MOV_R(ARM_R1, rn), ctx);
if (rm != ARM_R0)
    emit(ARM_MOV_R(ARM_R0, rm), ctx);
```
Reason:
The fix involves loading `rn` into `ARM_R1` before loading `rm` into `ARM_R0`. This ensures that `ARM_R0` retains its original value (the dividend) when `jit_udiv()` is called, preventing the situation where both the dividend and divisor are the same, thus correcting the division operation for `BPF_ALU | BPF_DIV | BPF_K` instructions.

